      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#0 · Frank Taylor's travelling image; Heidegger's world-picture passages (q012)",
          "title": "The picture arrives before the pieces",
          "italic": "The lid embodies the diagnostic: the world approached as though its possible appearances had already been cut by a maker whose picture requires only assembly.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The puzzle begins with its destination already visible. The maker sets out the edges, builds the frame, sorts the remaining pieces by marks promising a place within it; each successful fit confirms a small part of the anticipated whole. Yet the finished picture entered the work before the first piece was placed: it supplies the criterion by which every later placement will be judged. The maker can hesitate over a patch of colour while remaining entirely certain what",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "counts as completion; the lid decides which differences belong together, which edge is outside, and which apparent anomaly is merely a piece awaiting its correct position. Heidegger's world-picture passages historicise the diagnosis — world grasped as picture and the representer installed as its normative centre belong to one event. The lid can remain absent from discussion precisely because everything discussed has already been assigned a possible place beneath it.\n\nOccurrences: the lid picture (#0, reopened at #5→0); the frame and sorted pieces (#0); the criterion working silently (#0, #1).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
