      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#1 · the reconstruction requirement (quilt correction)",
          "title": "Travel changes what it means to fit",
          "italic": "The change demonstrates itself: pieces become local charts whose edges mark limits of usable description, and neighbours overlap rather than merely meet along a cut.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The puzzle travels into the world it claims to depict. Its maker encounters a turn the flat arrangement cannot preserve, a continuation beyond an edge, a view whose distortion changes with position. At first the completed assembly absorbs the difficulty as imperfection in the traveller's knowledge — but another piece is still judged under the same criterion. The change comes when the maker begins to record how a view was made: from where, across which region, under what projection, with which",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "omissions. Pieces become local charts; their edges mark limits of usable description; neighbours overlap rather than merely meet. Within an overlap the maker must explain how a position described here appears there; a difference between reports can disclose a change of coordinates, a difference of measurement, or an unresolved disagreement. The seam becomes an operative relation, and an atlas can be worked through: enter a chart, cross an overlap, learn what changed, return with the route available.\n\nOccurrences: the encountered turn and edge (#1); charts and overlaps (#1, made exact at #2); the return with the route available (#1, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
