      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · the torus-cover matheme; A17 toroidal circulation; A16",
          "title": "The torus loop returns with its winding",
          "italic": "The lift demonstrates local closure retaining a difference in the wider relation — the diagnosis concerns the lost winding relation, not a ban on ordinary movement.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The torus-cover matheme derives the next operation: T²=R²/Z², with (x,y)~(x+m,y+n) for integers (m,n). One surface address has infinitely many plane representatives; a small neighbourhood is accurately represented by a local lift, and the quotient tells how its other representatives are related. Follow the loop [2t,−t] from t=0 to t=1: it returns to [0,0] on the torus while its lift moves from (0,0) to (2,−1). The pair records winding — not the traveller's",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "entire experience or the timing of every step. Under the first puzzle's disk abstraction every loop is contractible: the diagnosis concerns the loss of the torus's independent, non-contractible winding classes, not a ban on movement. The four sides of the presenting square and the two generating loops have distinct offices from the quotient's one vertex, two edge classes and one face; these counts cannot be exchanged because a picture makes them look alike.\n\nOccurrences: the lift's displaced endpoint (#2b, shared image with the uroboros whole's γ); the disk abstraction's lack (#2b); the distinct counted offices (#2b).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
