      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#4 · the quilt's named image-unit; no NASA frame selected; A04/C09; A20; C38/C61",
          "title": "The planet appears, and the making of the picture returns",
          "italic": "The same image embodies both possibilities: breadth of view cannot by itself establish the authority of the account made through it — the question is what happens to position, instrument, production and measure.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Blue Marble enters at the programme's hinge between a final box-lid world-picture and a first diaphanous planetary image — the authored image-unit named in the quilt, not a newly selected NASA photograph; no frame, date, mission or credit has been selected, so none is supplied by inference. As a box-lid, the planetary picture settles in advance what the world is: \"planetary\" becomes the unexamined scale under which particular lives and claims are counted. The quilt's questions",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "reopen that completeness: whose planet, computed by whom, on whose gauge? The same image becomes diaphanous when its conditions remain readable in use — location and time, production and transformations inspectable, what lies outside the selected account mattering to the next judgment. A04/C09 ground the change; A20 tests whether the image can still be altered by what it claims to disclose; the Encounter/Region/Name/Count/Countenance/Account field extends the hinge at register 3.\n\nOccurrences: the box-lid and its silent criterion (#0, #4); the planetary image and its reopened questions (#4); the inspectable conditions (#4, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
