      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#5→0 · C39 MEF; the Homologia/Analogia field; A34; Bratton q029; M05, M30, M41, M42, M44",
          "title": "The atlas travels with the means to revise it",
          "italic": "The whole returns-to its movements with duties intact: the map-making operation travels alongside its map — sufficiently definite to guide the next step, sufficiently answerable for the journey to change where it leads.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The reconstructive technical proposal begins where the first puzzle finished. C39 defines the lenses and gauges through which an inquiry changes salience, evidence and judgment; a change of lens must change what the inquiry does. The quilt offers Mapper as a concrete research route — lens, cover, local clustering, nerve — with its choices retained so the representation stays answerable to its construction; a Mapper nerve is not automatically a manifold atlas. Sheaf methods offer local data, restriction maps, compatibility; a genuine obstruction remains a result to expose, not a proof that computation is",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "impossible nor an entailment of an ethical pledge. The authored surety comparison names the further responsibility where the current formal arrangement cannot supply the required continuation. Bratton's Agentworld brief tests the proposal: divergent world-models need a common procedural grammar through which disagreement becomes legible — explicit transitions, scope and obstruction are part of the atlas's response. The traveller opens the first picture again: its colours and fits have not lost their achievement; they can now be read with their frame, their missed continuations and the routes into other accounts.\n\nDeclared cross-story: torus lift shared with the uroboros whole's interposition scene (same matheme home, different whole offices). ↳ Occurrences: the reopened first picture (#0, #5→0); the surety gap (#5→0); the declared returns to M05/M30/M41/M42/M44 (#5→0).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
